Subject: Plan for the Cantor M2B Windows Sys Compile Probe Lock Revision

& [PlanIdentity] is implementation ordered
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-topology-abi-probe/0.2
  + [authority_required] is a valid 0.2 satisfaction signature

& [Step01] verify clean boundary
  + assert Cargo.lock pre-hash
  + assert Cargo.toml and probe file have no retained implementation delta

& [Step02] implement dependency
  + add the exact cfg(windows) target dependency and closed feature set

& [Step03] implement no-call probe
  + create one cfg(windows) integration test
  + bind five generated function items without calling or casting them
  + compare layouts, class codes, constants, and fingerprint

& [Step04] resolve and gate lock
  + allow Cargo to record the intended edge offline
  + require the exact one-line diff
  + require post-hash ff20148aa6ff3c2774d07d454bc900f4f81d5594bd8f8e49af2a43217b7ee73a
  + require 112 packages

& [Step05] static security scan
  + reject the unsafe token
  + reject each imported function in call-expression position
  + reject production Rust delta

& [Step06] focused verification
  + run Windows debug probe
  + run overflow-checked release probe
  + inspect exact direct feature tree

& [Step07] global verification
  + run workspace debug and overflow-checked release tests
  + run warnings-denied lint, release build, and rustdoc
  + run dependency audit and license/checksum review

& [Step08] evidence repair
  + discover every manifest binding Cargo.toml or Cargo.lock
  + regenerate affected manifests in predecessor order
  + update each dependent proof hash
  + verify clone portability and artifact hashes

& [Step09] close records
  + create solution and proof
  + update requirement matrix and support ledger
  + create completion review
  + update turn, file-change, fault, registry, reentry, and conversation surfaces

& [Step10] publish
  + commit implementation separately from proof where useful
  + push intentional checkpoints
  + do not claim runtime scanner or physical proof readiness
